RELATIONAL DECLARATION SPEC
reconstruction rule

AXIOM
  If undeclared, it does not exist.
  Implicit background is not a resource.
  Flux fills only what declarations already license.

TYPES
  Rel     declared relation
  Mode    S | I | D | Q
  Dyad    2-body relation          (2 -> 4 path = MFE)
  Triad   closed 3-mode structure  (2 -> 3 path = RDG)
  Flux    MFE generator            (waves, propagation, remainder)
  Q       admissibility / quotient / repair projector
  DeltaR  declared mismatch channel
  Sigma   projection back onto admissible structure

VARIABLES
  P0          locationless point
  R           declared relation
  S(G)        structure / skeleton / anchor
  I(G)        interaction / integration
  D(G)        dynamics / propagation
  G           RDG object
  Gamma_t     evolving relational geometry
  d_s         screening / finite-range influence
  D(P,Q)^2    emergent distance = (sum_i DeltaR_i)^2
  X_t         state at t
  X_{t+1}     repaired / updated state

FUNDAMENTALS
  1. Relations first. Objects, fields, geometry, time are derived.
  2. Nothing implicit. Hidden universe, identity, metric, negation,
     excluded middle, or default coordinates are not present.
  3. Two lifts
       2 -> 3  RDG   point -> counterpoint -> couple -> triad
                     modes S / I / D
       2 -> 4  MFE   couple -> mirror-couple -> 4-pole flux engine
  4. SID nesting
       S(G) subset I(G) subset D(G) subset G
       S constrains I; I constrains D
  5. Repair rule
       Repair works upward IFF structure S is preserved.
       Dyadic erasure != triadic re-lifting.
  6. Reconstruction
       Requires explicit initial conditions and assumptions.
       If Q admits Gamma(X_t): X_{t+1} = Gamma(X_t)
       Else:                  X_{t+1} = Sigma(Gamma(X_t))
  7. Flux generates the rest
       Flux is not a source of new primitives.
       It only generates what declared Rel / Mode already authorize.
  8. Truth tables
       Post-hoc freeze of a surviving dyadic fragment.
       Cannot invent missing generators, closures, or triad.
       Tabulate != declare.

TEST
  Write every assumption as Rel or Mode.
  If you cannot write it, it is not in the system.
  No later table puts it back.
